{
  "name": "alpha-layout",
  "description": "\u00a711.1 \u2014 the alpha-mode tier-0 layout, which ships today with no evidence behind it. The opaque row was rebalanced to L 28 @ 4 / C 15 @ 3; alpha mode still carries v0.6's L 20 @ 5 / C 9 @ 4 only because the photographic corpus has no transparency. Every arm is exactly 32 bytes (249-256 bits: 54 prefix + 9 alpha DC/scale + L*lb + 2*C*cb + 5*4 alpha AC). Alpha AC is held at the shipped 5 @ 4 so the question stays how luma and chroma should split the alpha-mode budget; SS11.3 sweeps the alpha fields themselves. Scored over three backdrops with a direct alpha-plane MAE, because a single white backdrop hides most alpha error. Every arm pins `alpha_ac_count` and `alpha_ac_bits` explicitly. A config that overrides only part of a layout inherits the rest from Tunables::DEFAULT, so when the default alpha allocation changed in \u00a711.3 these arms silently stopped being 32 bytes \u2014 the same class of drift the corpus pins exist to prevent, in the knob space rather than the corpus.",
